
import:
-----------
Terraform import is used to bring an existing infrastructure resource, created manually or by another process, under Terraform management.

For example, suppose you created an EC2 instance directly in the AWS Console. You can import it into Terraform so Terraform can manage it.

Step 1: Write the Terraform configuration
-----------------------------------------

resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  ami           = "ami-xxxxxxxx"
  instance_type = "t3.micro"
}

Step 2: Import the EC2 instance
-------------------------------

terraform import aws_instance.web i-0123456789abcdef0


Step 3: Verify the configuration
---------------------------------

terraform state list
terraform state show aws_instance.web
terraform plan
